{"study_accession":"PRJNA858412","secondary_study_accession":"SRP386240","title":"Transcriptome of human peripheral blood regulatory T cells with distinct ex vivo expansion profile","description":"The UCSF Treg cell therapy program manufactured over 60 human regulatory T cell (Treg) products under the GMP condition in support of 9 clinical trials between 2011 and 2021. These products were manufactured using two alternative protocols of either two rounds of polyclonal stimulations (PolyTregs) or first allogeneic B cell stimulation followed by polyclonal stimulation (arTregs). A high degree of individual variability in Treg expansion with both protocols was observed. RNA-seq analysis was performed on freshly isolated peripheral blood Tregs to identify transcriptome profile associated with Treg expansions. Overall design: A total of 19 individuals with sufficient archived pre-expansion PBMCs were selected for RNA-seq analysis. Among these, 6 were classified as high expanders, 6 were mid expanders, and 7 were low expanders. Tregs were purfied from cryopreserved PBMCs using FACS based on the phenotype of CD4+CD25+CD127lo/-. Total RNA was extracted for RNAseq.","pubmed":"36322627","geo_series":"","n_samples":19,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN29714803","study_accession":"PRJNA858412","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"ARTEMIS #6","description":"ARTEMIS #6","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6337483","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-04-28","attributes":[["source_name","Peripheral blood Tregs"],["group","arTreg low expansion"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR20140591","experiment_accession":"SRX16175644","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":33574344,"base_count":9420037294,"first_public":"2024-04-28","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM6337483: ARTEMIS #6 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labe